    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d291">

                <pb facs="0399" n="279" xml:id="pg279"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Cuban Minister to
                        Acting Secretary of State Adee.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Cuba</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-03-29"><hi rendition="#italic">March 29,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 201.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to the memorandum of your
                    Department of the 17th of January of this year, and to mine of the 19th of the
                    same month and year, I would like to know if, in view of the urgent condition of
                    Mr. Luciano F. Arestuche, to whom, as a grace, that Department is disposed to
                    grant $500 for injuries suffered at the hands of soldiers of the American Army,
                    it would be possible to deliver to me the said sum to have it reach the said
                    destitute individual.</p>
                <p>I avail, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales de
                    Quesada.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
